<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Juan Bosch</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1909">1909</a>–<a href="/years/2001">2001</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Juan Bosch was a Dominican writer and politician who founded the Dominican Revolutionary Party in exile during the Trujillo dictatorship. He won the first free elections after Trujillo's death in December 1962 but was overthrown by a military coup in September 1963. Supporters' attempt to restore him led to the civil war and US intervention of 1965.</p></div>
